Endpoint Returns <code>/livez</code> 200 as long as the api process serves requests. It doesn't check the store. Use it for the liveness probe. <code>/readyz</code> 200 when the api serves, isn't shutting down and its store answers within a second; 503 otherwise. Use it for the readiness probe and load balancers. <code>/status</code> The mode of the api, e.g. <code>{"mode":"normal"}</code>. <code>/metrics</code> Prometheus metrics, see below. <p>The probes follow the Kubernetes conventions: a store outage makes the api not ready (Kubernetes stops sending requests to it), but doesn't make Kubernetes restart it, which wouldn't fix the store. On SIGTERM the api returns 503 on <code>/readyz</code> for <code>--shutdown-delay</code>, so load balancers stop sending requests, and then finishes the running requests and stops. Keep <code>terminationGracePeriodSeconds</code> (30s by default) above the shutdown delay plus 10 seconds.</p> <pre><code>livenessProbe:
  httpGet: {path: /livez, port: 8080}
readinessProbe:
  httpGet: {path: /readyz, port: 8080}
</code></pre>
